The SystemOS union on "/" is one volume to iOS and macOS. The owner chain union-mounts the SystemOS volume over the root
volume, so files under "/" come from two APFS volumes and getfsstat lists two mounts on "/"; Apple CoreServices
(LaunchServices / FileIDTree / _MountInfoPrepare) aborts on two volumes with one device id or on a device id no mount lists.
As macOS-DroidVM's virt_union_top and UniXNU's macOS profile do, the root volume under the union is reported as the union:
getfsstat leaves the root volume out, and stat, statfs and getattrlist give the SystemOS volume's device id and statfs
(with MNT_UNION, which libc's opendir needs to merge and deduplicate the two layers; reported the other way round, readdir
listed the upper layer only, macOS run33).
--- a/bsd/vfs/vfs_subr.c
+++ b/bsd/vfs/vfs_subr.c
@@ -13504,3 +13504,22 @@
 {
 	return os_atomic_load(&vp->v_ext_flag, relaxed) & VE_APPENDONLY;
 }
